# Wave W17-AA (Route 219): bright sand — bright turquoise-shallows sand, gold flecks: a pale warm sand under bright shallow water, carrying gold flecks where the sun reaches the bottom, the south sea road’s own footing off Shingle beach (design: bright water, honest weather). Route 219’s own sand — split from its twin Route 220’s long sand by warmth entire (gold-flecked shallows vs sparse open-sea pale) and from the Maris lanes’ sands by light: this is Borea’s brightest lane, theirs run under southern cloud.
